{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 35, :comments ["<b>And you shall set the table.</b> The golden altar stands in the middle, drawn slightly toward the outside. The reason: since it is written 'the menorah opposite the table,' we require that they face each other. So they explained in tractate Yoma." "<b>And the menorah opposite the table.</b> To illuminate it. And so it is written in the perasha of BeHa'alotekha: 'אל מול פני המנורה יאירו שבעת הנרות' — upon the table, which is opposite the menorah, the seven lamps shall give light." "<b>On the south side of the tabernacle.</b> Light is always from the south, like the sun, which travels toward the south."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:00:40.786238228Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}